    alignUp(static_cast<std::size_t>(address), alignment)
);
return reinterpret_cast<T*>(aligned);
```

That's correct — three `static_cast`s and two `reinterpret_cast`s in the right places. Somewhere in transcription, both pointer-related casts got changed: the first one wrong-way (to `static_cast`, which we just fixed), and now this second one also wrong-way (to `reinterpret_cast`). Possibly an attempt at consistency that pulled them in opposite wrong directions.

The corrected version above is what should be in your real code. Same fix needed for `alignDown` — the body has the same structure, with the same casts in the same positions, just calling `alignDown` instead of `alignUp` on the integer.

